      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks have transformed precision frequency metrology and provide an exceptionally sensitive new way to measure time, gravity, and fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Katori introduced the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept and Ye made decisive experimental advances toward practical record-performance clocks.",
        "maturity": "The approach has been replicated extensively, attains extraordinary reproducible accuracy, and is now a durable international measurement platform.",
        "uncertainties": [
